From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:00:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 100/111] A selection dragged past the top or bottom of the
 preview scrolls it

While the button is held past the preview's top or bottom edge, the
preview scrolls that way every frame, faster the farther the pointer
is past the edge, and the selection follows to the text at the edge.
It stops on release; nothing runs while no drag is on. The preview
scrolls as for the user, so in the Split view the editor follows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

